gm-method: when recall surfaces a 'canonical sibling checkout is X not Y' claim, witness it by `git remote -v` + `git log --oneline -1` + package version on BOTH paths before trusting either - stale memories of which dev checkout is authoritative are a common drift. The newer-commit / higher-version checkout with the same origin is canonical NOW regardless of an older memo naming a different path. A consumer repo pinned to an OLD published version while the sibling source has advanced many patch versions is a real parity gap to plan, not noise. Read sibling-repo files by absolute path (Read/exec_js), never codesearch (indexes cwd only). require()-ing a sibling package.json by a /c/dev/... bash-style path fails under node on win32 - use forward-slash C:/dev/... or Read the file.